<title>USA: TABLE - Zitel Corp restated Q3 results.</title>
<headline>TABLE - Zitel Corp restated Q3 results.</headline>
<dateline>FREMONT, Calif. 1997-08-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>(In Thousands Except Per Share Data) (Unaudited)</p>
<p>				Three Months Ended  Nine Months Ended</p>
<p>				   6/30/97  6/30/96  6/30/97  6/30/96</p>
<p> Net sales			  $2,215  $1,911   $7,057  $6,501</p>
<p> Royalty revenue		   1,137   3,733    4,651  11,916</p>
<p>   Total revenue		   3,352   5,644   11,708  18,417</p>
<p> Cost of goods sold		1,707   1,780    6,243   4,819</p>
<p>Research &amp; development expenses</p>
<p>					 1,671   1,639    4,906   4,832</p>
<p>Selling, general and</p>
<p>  administrative expenses	3,291   1,974    8,789   5,756</p>
<p>Reduction in purchased development</p>
<p>					 6,600	--    6,600	--</p>
<p>   Operating income (loss)   (9,917)     251  (14,830)  3,010</p>
<p> Other (income) expense	 1,163  (1,612)     128  (3,125)</p>
<p>Income (loss) before</p>
<p>    income taxes		(11,080)   1,863  (14,958)  6,135</p>
<p>Provision (benefit) for income</p>
<p>  taxes			    (3,107)     717  (4,503)   2,362</p>
<p>   Net income (loss)	   (7,973)   1,146 (10,455)   3,773</p>
<p> Net income (loss) per share   (.52)     .07    (.69)     .24</p>
<p>Number of shares used in</p>
<p>  per share calculation	 15,280  15,782   15,157  15,596</p>
<p>NOTE: Restated earnings relect recent positions taken by the Securities and Exchange Commission and the Emerging Issues Task Force on the accounting of convertible debt. The new position requires certain debt to be expensed as an interest charge from the date of issuance to the first date of permitted conversion.</p>
</text>
